Your three **magnetic-field sign changes are correct**, including the axis limit:
\[
\mathbf B=\nabla\psi\times\nabla\phi
=-\frac{\psi_Z}{R}\hat{\mathbf e}_R+\frac{\psi_R}{R}\hat{\mathbf e}_Z,
\qquad B_Z(R=0)=\psi_{RR}.
\]
These align \(\mathbf B\) with the positive field-line tangent for increasing maps and \(\psi_R>0\). The Jacobian and basis signs should stay unchanged.

**One required change is missing:** [`curlbhat_func`](/home/maxwell-rosen/gkeyll/gyrokinetic/zero/mirror_grid_gen.c:72) still uses the old field direction. Consequently, its nonzero curl has the opposite sign from \(\nabla\times(\mathbf B/|\mathbf B|)\). Update its field and derivative definitions together:

```c
Br = -dpsidZ / r_curr;
Bz = dpsidR / r_curr;

dBrdR = -d2psidRdZ / r_curr - Br / r_curr;
dBrdZ = -d2psidZ2 / r_curr;
dBzdR = d2psidR2 / r_curr - Bz / r_curr;
dBzdZ = d2psidRdZ / r_curr;
```

The subsequent magnitude derivatives and curl formula remain valid.

The [header comment](/home/maxwell-rosen/gkeyll/gyrokinetic/zero/gkyl_mirror_grid_gen.h:18) and signed expectations in both [grid tests](/home/maxwell-rosen/gkeyll/gyrokinetic/unit/ctest_mirror_grid_gen.c:499) and [geometry tests](/home/maxwell-rosen/gkeyll/gyrokinetic/unit/ctest_gk_geometry_mirror.c:1723) also need updating.

Both test executables compiled. Current runs fail **13/21 grid tests and 2/4 geometry tests**; their expectations still encode the old field direction. This review did not modify your source files.

